                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Absolute peak of slasher combat.\nDante's combat is the best part of the game. A motorcycle-chainsaw, a hat that shoots orbs, style switches on the fly. The best character for combo variety.\nNero is snappy, but the disposable prosthetics mechanic, where you can't switch them on the fly without destroying the arm, is an ingenious Japanese crutch.\nV is easily the worst in terms of combat. You stand in a corner, mash 2 buttons while the familiars rack up SSS ranks for you. Boring to the point of yawning.\n\nIn this installment, Capcom simply spat in the faces of fans of 3 and 4. Lady, who carried the plot on her back in DMC3, and Trish, who literally has the appearance of Dante and Vergil's mother, were turned into objects of fanservice. Their entire role is to fall out of bosses completely naked and sit in the background of the van. They literally shoved a lightbulb up Lady's ass.\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3701757523\n\nThe RE Engine delivers a cool photorealistic image and runs stably without FPS drops, BUT the level designers died halfway through development. The first third of the game is a grey ruined city, and the remaining two-thirds are endless, identical, nauseatingly brown tree intestines. By the end, these monotonous meat tubes make you want to puke.",
